NAME
    rotate_keys - rewrite some of your files' blocks

SYNOPSIS
    rotate_keys

DESCRIPTION
    Despite its name, rotate_keys changes no key. It reads and writes
    back the first four blocks of each file you own, stopping after 64
    blocks in all, and reports how many it rewrote. Each block is sealed
    again under the same per-block key with a fresh random nonce, so the
    ciphertext changes and the key does not. It needs a volume unlocked
    by a login.

    This is recorded as a limitation (LIMITATIONS 2.26); until it is
    rebuilt or withdrawn, do not rely on it for anything.

SECURITY
    The kernel requires the console capability, a file key for your login
    and the storage capability.

SEE ALSO
    passwd(1)
